## Learn a binary decision tree

Exercise files: [decision-trees.lp](../assets/decision-trees/decision-trees.lp) · [instance-06-05.lp](../assets/decision-trees/instances/instance-06-05.lp) · [instance-06-05.json](../assets/decision-trees/solutions/instance-06-05.json).

```elixir
workdir = Course.workspace(Path.expand("../assets/decision-trees", __DIR__))
```

Construct a tree with the requested odd number of nodes that classifies every training example. Internal nodes test attributes and leaves carry class labels. Do not repeat an attribute along a root-to-leaf path or give two sibling leaves the same class.

Complete the starter encoding before comparing its projected models with the supplied solution data.

### Keep the data contract

Read `example/2`, `holds/2` and `n`. Show `edge/2`, `decision/2` and `positive/1`. Node 1 is the root; children form consecutive, increasing ID pairs. The lower child is the false branch, and earlier parents receive earlier child pairs.

### Develop and check the encoding

Complete the editable encoding below. Compare its shown atom sets with the JSON answers in `solutions`; `optimal_cost` records a proven optimum when present. Download your edits before cleanup.

